<id/09/0928/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Marmalade"@en ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_sugars_sweeteners/#concept> ;
    skos:definition "a confection; preserved or sweetened fruit. Scotch marmalade is presumed to be of oranges; and there are also marmalades of lemon, quince, and shaddock. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 253]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated classification (group=grp_sugars_sweeteners; processing_state=manufactured): Marmalade is a sugar preserve (cf. Succades, htc:0464). Layer-1 observations: 29 rows, 1811–1846. Series: KEW_CUST 4 ×29. Units: Lbs. (Pounds) ×29. Top routes: Canada → England ×14; Canada → Great Britain ×6; Canada → London ×5; Newfoundland → England ×2."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <id/scheme/#resource> ;
    skos:notation "0928" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Marmalade"@en ;
